# Gerotech — multi-agent sync (Cursor + Cline)

This repo is edited in **Cursor** and **VS Code (Cline)**. Stay aligned via git + shared files.

## Every session — read first

1. `.clinerules` — live session state, blockers, recent decisions
2. `JOURNAL.md` — newest entry first
3. `git log -5 --oneline`

Also useful: `AGENTS.md`, `design-spec.md`, `docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `cline-project-handoff.md`

## Every session — write before ending

1. Prepend a short entry to `JOURNAL.md` (date, agent, what changed, loose ends)
2. Update **Current Session State** in `.clinerules` (last updated, active agent, last commit)

## Code conventions (do not drift)

- Static HTML/CSS/JS only — no frameworks or build tools
- CSS order: `tokens.css` → `components.css` → `layout.css` → **`elevated.css`**
- Navigo font kit `lqh7ybe` — **400 + 700** in kit; tokens ready for **500** when Matt adds Medium
- BEM classes; brand colors only in `tokens.css`
- Unsplash placeholders OK (comment each img); verify URLs — some 404 over time
- Hero + CTA photo bands: left-aligned, left gradient overlay (matches homepage)
- Interior heroes: all sub-pages **`.page-hero`** (homepage slide pattern); per-page `<img class="slide__bg">` in HTML
- Never guess open client decisions
- **WP Engine Dev:** theme-only push to `gerotechdev`; never Production; never Local DB. F1 image `haas-f1-team.jpg`. Read `.clinerules` pickup block.
- **Site Content editor (header/menus/footer ACF):** four screens; layout fields hidden via `gerotech-advanced` (reveal with `&advanced=1`), **never removed** — a removed repeater sub-field scrambles on reorder. No new-tab toggles: external hosts auto new-tab. Labels written for the client. Items 7–11 in `AGENTS.md` are **blocked on client/design decisions** — don't start them. Full plan: `AGENTS.md` → "Site Content editor".

